\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Webshare: Export stems\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Export the time selection as individual stems plus one combined mix. Top-level tracks are exported by default; toggle any track in the panel. Optionally writes a Markdown export log (YAML front matter) next to the files.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Requires ReaImGui} (ReaTeam Extensions repository). Restart REAPER after installing it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 How to use\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Actions \u8594 ? Show action list..., filter {\f1 webshare}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Run {\b Script: Webshare - Export stems.lua} to open the panel\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Make a time selection, check the ticks, click {\b Export}\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Files go to {\f1 Exports/<project>/<date time>/} next to the project file. Full documentation: https://github.com/sastraxi/reaper-webshare\par}
}
